                <pb facs="0496" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg424"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Telegram.—Translation from the Official
                        Journal of June 5, 1882.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Citizen Secretary of War</hi>: A fight was had with
                    the hand of Ju at daybreak on the 26th, in the San Diego woods, in which
                    thirty-six Indians were killed and ten were taken prisoners; fifty animals were
                    also captured. The rest of the band scattered over the Sierra Madre and is being
                    already tenaciously pursued.</p>
                <closer><signed>C. FUERO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
